<div class="theme-admonition theme-admonition-warning admonition_xJq3 alert alert--warning"><div class=admonitionHeading_Gvgb><span class=admonitionIcon_Rf37><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path fill-rule=evenodd d="M8.893 1.5c-.183-.31-.52-.5-.887-.5s-.703.19-.886.5L.138 13.499a.98.98 0 0 0 0 1.001c.193.31.53.501.886.501h13.964c.367 0 .704-.19.877-.5a1.03 1.03 0 0 0 .01-1.002L8.893 1.5zm.133 11.497H6.987v-2.003h2.039v2.003zm0-3.004H6.987V5.987h2.039v4.006z"/></svg></span>warning</div><div class=admonitionContent_BuS1><p>Google Chrome and Microsoft Edge have switched to a <a href=https://developer.chrome.com/docs/chromium/headless target=_blank rel="noopener noreferrer" class="">new headless mode</a> implementation that is closer to a regular headed mode. This differs from <a href=https://developer.chrome.com/blog/chrome-headless-shell target=_blank rel="noopener noreferrer" class="">chromium headless shell</a> that is used in Playwright by default when running headless, so expect different behavior in some cases. See <a href=https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/issues/33566 target=_blank rel="noopener noreferrer" class="">issue #33566</a> for details.</div></div>
